  "body": "Untrusted Transfer admission can currently bypass caller authorization on exact replay, synthesize original Parent evidence from the Event, and reconstruct an endpoint declaration from transported rows. This documentation-only Task D6 freezes an implementable I6 contract to close reproduced I5-A1/B1/C1, preserve D1 rollback, and replace F1's one-trigger inspection with a fail-closed both-fence contract. It does not implement or enable Transfer.\n\n**Design Author freeze for a separate non-Author review. No independent PASS or product acceptance is claimed.**\n\n### Stack and exact freeze\n\nThe owner explicitly selected newest **#133** after live discovery, superseding the assignment's exact-#132 base. Live #130\u2013#132 and main matched the supplied initial coordinates; no existing I6 design PR was found in two searches.\n\n- Base: `fix/adr0032-host-runtime-20261022` / #133 at **`f16e5b1713bde9a2f18263a25397c4b450fd5773`**, tree `6bfa580baafa9f6a117b7a0b610c4e65cd031b86`.\n- Author branch: `docs/adr0031-i6-boundary-contract-20261022`.\n- Frozen Author HEAD: **`418ee68046fdfd03a0e84cc840e5d52fce176b81`**.\n- Frozen Author tree: **`476d32923c9be5e3b60e4e17c8828e3646611c43`**.\n- One commit; sole parent is the exact #133 HEAD above.\n- #132 ancestor: `a022dd3efb9c8116cf9dc0abc13ab1d5bbc88e37`, tree `1fa9c2624a3913d97439f16fcd6bc8641c56b17f`. All 13 requested product modules are blob-identical between #132 and #133.\n- Main remains `cb532242c7aa86c6af5b6232b71c0906ea38f5c5`.\n\n### Contract and inventory\n\nExactly **four Markdown files, +1,026 / -0** relative to #133:\n\n| File | Change |\n| --- | --- |\n| [I6 wire/admission/Exchange contract](https://github.com/TakashiSasaki/git-repo-db/blob/418ee68046fdfd03a0e84cc840e5d52fce176b81/docs/implementation/adr0031-i6-wire-admission-exchange.md) | New, 490 lines; R01\u2013R19 |\n| [Canonical vectors and adversarial tests](https://github.com/TakashiSasaki/git-repo-db/blob/418ee68046fdfd03a0e84cc840e5d52fce176b81/docs/implementation/adr0031-i6-vectors-and-tests.md) | New, 268 lines; concrete V01\u2013V09 and T01\u2013T27 |\n| [Source map, implementation graph and review handoff](https://github.com/TakashiSasaki/git-repo-db/blob/418ee68046fdfd03a0e84cc840e5d52fce176b81/docs/implementation/adr0031-i6-change-map-and-handoff.md) | New, 259 lines; findings traceability, exact proposed files/APIs/evidence per stage |\n| `docs/implementation/context-resource-design-handoff.md` | Nine-line current entrypoint; earlier text/evidence untouched |\n\nFreezes v5-only wire/version refusal, all seven identification columns, independent complete Parent/Event originals, explicit pre-filter Provider endpoint declarations in the existing nine-key scope, mandatory locally bound AdmissionContext with current permission checks before replay, bounded whole-unit closure, ordered Relations/Collections and genuine terminals, Source positives/Coverage preservation, late/reverse/selective Exchange and no automatic replay. Identifies the legacy Exchange native-Parent registration loop, stripped identification and Transfer-before-Parent import order.\n\nProposed stack: I6-A secure domain/admission \u2192 independent A review \u2192 I6-B generalized codec \u2192 independent B review \u2192 I6-C Provider/Selective Exchange routes \u2192 independent C review \u2192 I7 recovery/G-R1 \u2192 I8 Transfer query/Search \u2192 independent integrated/artifact/regression gate \u2192 separately authorized both-fence retirement. Basic I8 generic reads may start after B. No genuine new owner-level decision identified; engineering choices and their recommendations are explicit.\n\n### Validation and limits\n\n- `python scripts/ci_execute.py reports`: **457 files passed**.\n- `python scripts/check_sqlite_validation_policy.py`: **0 violations**.\n- Staged/exact-parent whitespace and diff-scope checks passed.\n- Supplemental strict UTF-8/nonempty/fence checks, **27 local links/anchors**, **five JSON blocks**, inner canonical JSON/scoped identity reconstruction checks passed.\n- AST inspection verified the inherited exact outer field set; Git blob comparison verified all 13 requested product modules across #132/#133.\n- Protected source/tests/DDL, accepted ADRs, historical evidence, workflows/dependencies, AGENTS.md and skills have empty base-to-feature diffs. Working tree clean at freeze.\n- No product pytest, distribution build, new SQL execution or release validation was run for this documentation-only delta. Planned vectors are specifications. Historical 79 regression non-successes remain disclosed; later stages must preserve or honestly reconcile each node/phase/refusal without skip, xfail, assertion omission or narrowed selection.\n- New execution instructions use only the selected environment Python's actual SQLite under ADR 0032; product capability/WAL safety floors remain unchanged.\n- [Hosted tests run 39865183547, attempt 1](https://github.com/TakashiSasaki/git-repo-db/actions/runs/39865183547) **passed** both `sqlite-policy` and documentation-only `offline` jobs for this exact Author HEAD. Actual test merge `3ca6ec4dd2358c0434c7a33ad47095af338b2999` has parents exact #133 + Author HEAD and the same feature tree `476d32923c9be5e3b60e4e17c8828e3646611c43`.\n- Actual log receipt ZIP verified: **14,738 bytes**, SHA-256 `4d1f8f4482b1af86a5a7bf523ebde8f93a85c5087da98a870c8b121474d2c120`; all **10 indexed payload entries** match byte lengths/hashes, and feature/test-merge/tree/run/attempt bindings match. Manifest says `development_checks_passed`, `full_acceptance=false`, **0 executed product pytest IDs / 211 acceptance files unexecuted**. Product runtime, schema and installed-artifact lanes were skipped by the documentation-only plan. Measured hosted Python 3.12.15 / SQLite 3.53.1 is runtime identity, not new product acceptance.\n\nRead-only review instructions are in the handoff. Review separately against the frozen Author HEAD, add independent counterexamples for A1/B1/C1, and report findings without editing this Author branch. Material corrections require a new commit and re-review.\n\nPRs #129\u2013#133, their branches/reviews/frozen evidence and accepted ADR bodies are unchanged. Both packaged SQL Transfer fences and ordinary product refusals remain. No merge, deploy, release, P8 or real Provider/catalog operation.",
